<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    <details open>
      <summary>I have lipedema. Will these help?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">They're made for lipedema legs. The medical-grade graduated compression supports your lymphatic drainage, helping move the fluid that pools in lipedema tissue, which eases the heaviness, aching and that tight, "full" feeling. And because they're comfortable enough to wear all day, you get the consistent support that actually makes a difference. They don't cure lipedema (nothing does), but they help you manage the daily symptoms.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I'm stage 2 or 3. Will these still work?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Yes. They're cut for real lipedema proportions at every stage, up to 5XL. If your doctor has restricted compression for you, please check with them first.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What if I order the wrong size?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">It happens! Just reach out and we'll send you a replacement size right away.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How are these different from my prescribed compression?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Same graduated-compression principle, built the way Japanese women wear compression every day: soft, breathable, easy to pull on and discreet under normal clothes, so you actually wear them. If your specialist has prescribed a specific medical compression class, keep following that; many women wear Sira Sculpt as their comfortable everyday layer.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does this actually help lymphatic drainage?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Yes, that's the core of how it works. Graduated compression gently supports the movement of lymph fluid up and out of your legs as you move, a bit like a wearable version of manual lymphatic drainage (MLD) massage. It won't replace MLD or your treatment plan, but wearing it all day keeps that gentle support going between appointments, which is exactly what pooling, heavy lipedema legs need.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will they cure lipedema or remove the fat?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">No, and be wary of anything that claims to. Lipedema has no cure, and compression won't remove the fat. What Sira Sculpt does is ease the daily pain, heaviness and full feeling, and give you compression you'll actually keep on. Always follow your treatment plan and your specialist's advice.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I really wear them all day?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Yes, that's the whole point. They're designed to be soft and breathable enough to wear from morning to night, which is exactly what makes them work.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What about bathroom breaks?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">They pull down and back up in seconds. The stretch recovery means no wrestling, even on the fifth trip of the day.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Are they easy to put on?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Much easier than medical flat-knit stockings. The stretch fabric slides on without a fight. No rubber gloves or gadgets needed.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do they roll down or dig in?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">No. The wide, high waistband sits flat over your stomach without digging into tender tissue, and stays put through a full day of sitting, standing and walking.</div>
    </details>
    
    <details>
      <summary>Can I order more than one in different sizes or colors?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Yes. Add each color and size you want to your cart; every pair ships from our US warehouse.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What are they made of? Are they see-through?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">A dense knit of 90% polyamide and 10% elastane. It stays fully opaque when you squat, bend or sit, so they read as regular black leggings, not tights.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How firm is the compression?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">A gentle, comfort-grade hold: noticeably firmer than fashion leggings, gentler than prescribed flat-knit stockings. It's firmest at the ankle and eases up the thigh, so your legs feel supported and lighter without the squeeze that hurts tender skin.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I wear them during pregnancy?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Many women wear gentle compression during pregnancy, but every pregnancy is different. Please check with your doctor first.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I wash them?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Machine wash cold and let them air dry. The compression and shape hold up wash after wash, so they're ready to wear every day.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is the 90-day money-back guarantee?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">If you aren't happy with your purchase, send them back within 90 days for a full refund. No questions asked.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How long does shipping take?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">We ship from our warehouse in the USA, so orders arrive in 2-3 business days. Any questions? Reach us through the <a href="/pages/contact">contact page</a>.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>When will I feel a difference?<span class="plus">+</span></summary>
      <div class="ans">Many women feel lighter and less achy the very first day. The real benefit builds as you wear them consistently, which is finally realistic when they're this comfortable.</div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

